<section class="bugs">
	<div class="wrap">
		<h2>This design removes a whole class of client bugs.</h2>
		<div class="grid">
			<div class="item">
				<div class="title">No release call to forget</div>
				<div class="body">The lock is released whenever your function returns — or panics.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="item">
				<div class="title">No session id to persist and lose</div>
				<div class="body">The connection is the session. Nothing to store, nothing to leak.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="item">
				<div class="title">No lock without a live process</div>
				<div class="body">If the process dies, the kernel closes the socket, and the lock moves on.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

